        "notes": "Published NASA/JPL/DLR processed color from Galileo in May 2001, registered to the controlled USGS map. About 8 km per source pixel near the disk center; detail becomes coarser toward the edge. This is display color, not calibrated I/F or albedo. Only views within 65° of the surface normal are retained; gray grid marks the rest of the globe. Photographed shading and color fringes remain; added globe lighting is approximate.",
